3035309998368e5c52da3dfc79255650337bae"},"seconds":51.12883520126343,"seed":792152318969961804,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b})$, let's start by using the distributive property of the cross product over vector addition and scalar multiplication:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = \\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a}) - \\mathbf{c} \\times (2 \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out the scalars:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a}) = 3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (2 \\mathbf{b}) = 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\n\nGiven the properties of the cross product, we know:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c}).\n\\]\n\nUsing the provided values:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) = 3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we find:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).\n\\]\n\nUsing the provided values:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = 2 \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nFinally, we combine these results:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 + 2 \\\\ -21 - 14 \\\\ -6 + 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve for $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b})$, let's start by using the distributive property of the cross product over vector addition and scalar multiplication:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = \\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a}) - \\mathbf{c} \\times (2 \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out the scalars:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a}) = 3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (2 \\mathbf{b}) = 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\n\nGiven the properties of the cross product, we know:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c}).\n\\]\n\nUsing the provided values:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) = 3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we find:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).\n\\]\n\nUsing the provided values:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = 2 \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nFinally, we combine these results:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 + 2 \\\\ -21 - 14 \\\\ -6 + 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]","id":"precalculus:429"}
